1. Built-in data structures:

These are the fundamental Python data structures.

No.	Data structure - Python type - Mutable?

1	Integer - int - No
2	Floating point - float - No
3	Boolean - bool - No
4	String - str - No
5	List - list - Yes

6	Tuple - tuple - No
7	Set - set - Yes
8	Frozen Set - frozenset - No
9	Dictionary - dict - Yes
10	Bytes - bytes - No

11	Byte Array - bytearray - Yes
12	Range - range - No

Note: int, float, and bool are scalar types rather than 
conventional data structures. 
They are included for completeness.

-----------------------------------------------------
2. Specialized data structures – Python Standard Library:

Python provides several additional data structures 
through built-in modules.

No.	Data structure - Module - Purpose

1	Dynamic Array - array - Typed arrays
2	Double-ended Queue - collections.deque - Queue and deque
3	Counter - collections.Counter - Frequency counting
4	Ordered Dictionary - collections.OrderedDict - Ordered key-value storage
5	Default Dictionary - collections.defaultdict - Dictionary with default values

6	Named Tuple - collections.namedtuple - Named fields in tuples
7	Chain Map - collections.ChainMap - Multiple dictionary views
8	Heap / Priority Queue - heapq - Priority-based operations
9	Queue - queue.Queue - Thread-safe FIFO
10	LIFO Queue - queue.LifoQueue - Thread-safe stack

11	Priority Queue - queue.PriorityQueue - Thread-safe priority queue
12	Simple Queue - queue.SimpleQueue - Simplified thread-safe FIFO
13	Binary Search - bisect - Sorted sequence operations

